*** PRELUDE
*** A2b-nan-gating — NaN can never appear in a Maude value; Infinity ops stay unreduced
*** Infinity is built with float("Infinity") (reduces to Infinity on BOTH sides) so the diff isolates the
*** NaN-manufacturing bug rather than tnk's separate Infinity-literal parse gap.
red in CONVERSION : float("Infinity") - float("Infinity") .
red in CONVERSION : float("Infinity") * 0.0 .
red in CONVERSION : float("Infinity") / float("Infinity") .
red in CONVERSION : float("Infinity") rem 2.0 .
*** regression guard: these are already unreduced on both sides
red in CONVERSION : sqrt(-1.0) .
red in CONVERSION : 1.0 / 0.0 .
